#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:287
msgid "Flash Encryption"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:291
msgid ""
"Enabling flash encryption limits the options for further updates of your "
"device. Before using this feature, make sure to read the entire page and "
"fully understand the implications."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:297
msgid ""
"Enabling flash encryption will increase the size of the bootloader, which "
"might require updating partition table offset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:301
msgid ""
"Flash encryption is intended for encrypting the contents of the ESP32's off-"
"chip flash memory. Once this feature is enabled, firmware is flashed as "
"plaintext, and then the data is encrypted in place on the first boot. As a "
"result, physical readout of flash will not be sufficient to recover most "
"flash contents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:303
msgid ""
"It's recommended to read the official `Flash Encryption Programming Guide "
"<https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v5.4.1/esp32/security/flash-"
"encryption.html>`_ to understand the overall workflow before getting "
"started. Here's an adapted version of that page that uses PlatformIO "
"packages to enable the Flash Encryption Feature on ESP32 ECO V3 target:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../frameworks/espidf_extra.rst:305
msgid ""
"Ensure that you have an ESP32 device with default Flash Encryption eFuse "
"settings as shown in `Relevant eFuses <https://docs.espressif.com/projects/"
"esp-idf/en/v5.4.1/esp32/security/flash-encryption.html#flash-encryption-"
"efuse>`_. At this point, the Flash Encryption must not be already enabled on "
"the chip."
